# The build compiles ./cmd/server and nothing else, so the context is an
# allowlist rather than a list of things to keep out. A denylist has to be
# updated every time something new appears in the repository, and the cost of
# forgetting is a secret baked into an image layer: before this file existed,
# COPY . . put the live .env, the whole .git directory and a .DS_Store into the
# builder image, and the .env carried a real API token.
*

!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/
!internal/

# Nothing below is needed to compile, and some of it must never be shipped:
#   .env, .env.*      secrets, including the live one
#   .git              history, ~10MB, and every secret ever committed
#   .github, *.md     project furniture
#   .DS_Store, ~$*    editor and finder droppings
#   docker-compose.yml, Dockerfile   describe the build, not inputs to it
#
# Adding a package under a new top-level directory means adding it above. The
# build fails loudly in that case rather than silently shipping something.
